<h1>Permission to Test & Security Assessment Authorization Agreement</h1>

<p><strong>Effective Date:</strong> _____________________</p>

<p>This Permission to Test & Security Assessment Authorization Agreement (“Agreement”) is entered into by and between:</p>

<p><strong>Authorizing Entity:</strong> ___________________________________________<br>
Address: ___________________________________________<br>
Representative Name & Title: ___________________________________________</p>

<p>and</p>

<p><strong>Security Assessor:</strong> ___________________________________________<br>
Address: ___________________________________________</p>

<h2>1. Purpose</h2>
<p>
The Authorizing Entity grants express written permission to the Security Assessor to conduct
security testing and vulnerability assessments against the systems identified below.
This authorization is intended to provide lawful consent for activities that may otherwise
be restricted under applicable state or federal computer access laws.
</p>

<h2>2. Scope of Authorized Systems</h2>
<div class="boxed">
    <p>Domains: ___________________________________________</p>
    <p>IP Address Ranges: ___________________________________________</p>
    <p>Applications: ___________________________________________</p>
    <p>Cloud Environments: ___________________________________________</p>
    <p>Other Assets: ___________________________________________</p>
</div>

<h2>3. Authorized Testing Activities</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Vulnerability scanning</li>
    <li>Configuration review</li>
    <li>Authentication and access control testing</li>
    <li>Network service enumeration</li>
    <li>Web application testing</li>
    <li>Controlled exploitation of confirmed vulnerabilities</li>
</ul>

<p>
All testing shall be conducted in good faith, limited strictly to the systems listed above,
and in a manner designed to minimize operational disruption.
</p>

<h2>4. Prohibited Activities</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Intentional denial-of-service attacks</li>
    <li>Data destruction</li>
    <li>Testing outside the defined scope</li>
    <li>Accessing third-party systems not explicitly authorized</li>
</ul>

<h2>5. Legal Authorization</h2>
<p>
The Authorizing Entity affirms that it owns or has lawful authority over the systems
identified in Section 2 and grants explicit consent for the Security Assessor
to access and test those systems solely within the defined scope.
</p>

<p>
This Agreement is intended to serve as documented authorization under applicable
computer access statutes and shall remain in effect until revoked in writing.
</p>

<h2>6. Confidentiality</h2>
<p>
Any findings, vulnerabilities, or sensitive data discovered during testing shall be treated
as confidential and disclosed only to authorized representatives of the Authorizing Entity.
</p>

<h2>7. Indemnification & Liability</h2>
<p>
The parties acknowledge that security testing carries inherent risk.
The Security Assessor agrees to exercise reasonable professional care.
The Authorizing Entity agrees that authorized activities conducted within scope
shall not constitute unauthorized access.
</p>

<h2>8. Term & Revocation</h2>
<p>
This authorization begins on the Effective Date and remains valid until:
</p>
<ul>
    <li>The agreed testing window concludes; or</li>
    <li>Written revocation is provided by the Authorizing Entity.</li>
</ul>

<h2>9. Governing Law</h2>
<p>
This Agreement shall be governed by the laws of the State of _____________________
and applicable federal law.
</p>

